@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:security] seed-rbac-converges-on-rerun
seed_rbac.ts MUST set every Role row's permissions to the seeded list for that role, creating the row
when missing, and MUST create each missing Permission row once, so a second run changes no row. It
MUST give the seeded list to a user only when that user's stored permissions are null or empty, and
MUST NOT change any other user, any Role isActive flag, any Permission it did not create, or any table
other than permissions, roles and users. OWNER and ADMIN receive "*". It MAY be rerun, but every run
discards manual edits to Role.permissions. verify_rerun_safety.ts, run in CI, fails unless the second run is a no-op.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:security] reception-backfill-only-adds-permissions
backfill_reception_permissions.ts MUST add the RECEPTION defaults to the RECEPTION Role row and to
every user whose role is RECEPTION, keeping each permission already stored, and MUST NOT remove a
permission or change a user of any other role, any other Role row, or any table other than roles and
users. It MUST set the RECEPTION Role active, and it MUST replace unparseable stored permissions with
the defaults. It MAY be rerun, because a second run adds nothing. A rerun does not undo a removal
stored in users.revokedPermissions, where Role & Permissions records an unticked permission: this
script does not touch that column and it wins over the stored permissions. The header comment, which
says only null or invalid permissions are targeted, is wrong: every RECEPTION user is merged.
verify_rerun_safety.ts, run in CI, fails unless the second run is a no-op.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:security] reception-inventory-merge-only-adds-permissions
merge_reception_full_inventory.ts MUST add the thirty inventory:* permissions to the RECEPTION Role
row and to every user whose role is RECEPTION, keeping each permission already stored, and MUST NOT
remove a permission, change another role's users or Role rows, or touch any inventory item,
transaction or stock quantity. It MUST set the RECEPTION Role active and replace unparseable stored
permissions with the thirty. It MAY be rerun, because a second run adds nothing. A rerun does not
undo a removal stored in users.revokedPermissions, where Role & Permissions records an unticked
permission: this script does not touch that column and it wins.
verify_rerun_safety.ts, run in CI, fails unless the second run is a no-op.

@cc [owner:nareshshah139,label:security;target] rbac-scripts-confirm-target-database
seed_rbac.ts, backfill_reception_permissions.ts and merge_reception_full_inventory.ts MUST NOT write
permissions to a database the operator has not confirmed, for example by printing the database host
and name and requiring an explicit flag for a non-loopback host. This is a target obligation, not a
pass claim: each script writes to whatever DATABASE_URL points at and prints nothing about the target.
